Hi Michelle and Divya,

I have finished asking the shift leads about all six seats. The attached IT f=
ollow-up sets out the reasons and next actions by pilot code. P25 and P26 mis=
sed practice because it overlapped the shift change; P27 and P28 were viewing=
 roles. P29 was on leave and P30's lead sent on their behalf.

We can set up a night-shift practice for P25 and P26. I would like to check h=
ow the pilot codes correspond to the production seat codes against the roster=
 I hold when Divya and I meet on the 27th. I will also check P29's role after=
 return and prepare backup sender coverage for P30. I am not recommending P27=
 or P28 for the first roster.

Thanks,
Lawrence

On March 19, 2025, Michelle Whitaker wrote:
> For each seat, was the person expected to send operational messages, and we=
re they able to attend a practice slot? Who should confirm the person's role =
for April? Please reply using the seat codes rather than names. That will giv=
e Divya and you a useful starting point for the first production roster check.

